    g=s['enumeration_gate'];add();add(f"The complete-universe gate took **{g['aggregate_cpu_seconds']:.6f} CPU seconds** and {g['wall_seconds']:.6f} wall seconds under the frozen aggregate 120 CPU-second ceiling. A general future-row blocked-bit enumerator generated each N13 leaper family. An independent ordinary-queen three-bitmask enumerator produced all **14,200 N12** and **73,712 N13** queen boards; literal leaper-pair filtering exactly matched both known complete N12 sources and both new N13 target arrays. Unique boards and complete array equality were required. No partial universe was used.")
    add();add(f"Complete input preparation enumerates all 377 one/two/three-clue subsets per N13 solution and counts distinct keys. Vectorized generation agrees exactly with literal subset enumeration on the first 17 boards of each family. Input enumeration took {s['input_preparation']['aggregate_cpu_seconds']:.6f} CPU seconds and {s['input_preparation']['wall_seconds']:.6f} wall seconds. All CPU preparation, including source designs and source calibration inputs, took {s['cpu_preparation']['wall_seconds']:.6f} wall seconds and {s['cpu_preparation']['aggregate_child_cpu_seconds']:.6f} aggregate child CPU seconds, before the GPU deadline.")
    add();add('The model producer recomputes canonical source-offset counts, marginal exposures, primitive homogeneous zero-count lines and grouped coefficients from each complete source bank. It receives no family leaper rule. Each inferred line shares a coefficient; each remaining finite offset has its own; one shared unary is fitted. The unchanged hash-pinned H3u PL objective exactly aggregates 298 clue subsets per source board using occupied/empty free-cell multiplicities 231/298. Every source pattern receives equal weighting within its family. The two source counts differ (472 versus 1,304), so this is neither a matched-sample-count comparison nor two source-bank draws from a shared population.')
    add();add('BP AdamW uses zero initialization, 4,000 updates, learning rate 0.3 and the original cosine schedule denominator 4,000, decay 0.01, betas (0.9,0.999), epsilon 1e-8, float32, TF32 disabled and no preconditioner. Each family has a 120-second fit ceiling. Finite parameters, a positive native source margin and strictly positive retained/transferred F weights are required. Literal expanded-clue PL/gradient checks and actual-source CPU/GPU loss/gradient checks precede each fit; source counts, exposure, grouping and every transferred edge are independently reconstructed.')
    add();add('| Family index | Source retained F offsets | Source native minimum margin | Source temperature unit | Target true / false / missed F pairs | Fit seconds |');add('|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|')
    for r in s['source_models']:add(f"| {r['bank']} | {r['source_retained_offsets']} | {r['native_source_delta']:.6f} | {r['unit']:.9f} | {r['target_true_forbidden_pairs']} / {r['target_false_forbidden_pairs']} / {r['target_missed_forbidden_pairs']} | {r['fit_seconds']:.6f} |")
    add();add('The positive-F derivative retains zero-count finite source offsets whose marginal exposure is at least ln(264/0.01), union inferred lines. It keeps learned positive coefficients on F, zeroes unary/off-support weights, extends lines to N13, and assigns newly representable off-line offsets zero. Source temperature is the float32 mean learned coefficient across unique retained canonical source offsets. Its certificate is an exact integer zero count of occupied F edges, including given–given pairs, with q=13 preserved. This derivative differs from the native soft fitted energy.')
    add();add('Each family’s source calibration uses 4,096 unique N13-shaped inputs derived only from its N12 source bank: 2 one-clue, 205 two-clue and 3,889 three-clue inputs, seeds 2026112810/2026112811. The arbitrary reference cap is 20,000; the fixed permutation grid is 8,000/12,000/16,000. Source streams 101/102/103 run on both physical GPUs with balanced configuration order, yielding six timings per configuration. A fixed closest-median rule selects a cap within ±5%; at most one deterministic interpolated cap, rounded to a multiple of 128, is allowed. No extrapolation or additional tuning is available. Calibration does not open target arrays, keys or labels, and never computes target accuracy.')
    add();add('| Family index | Source selection status | Permutation cap | Source median ratio | Source ratio 5th/95th endpoints | Interpolation |');add('|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|')
