    add();add('The source point-median gate is separate from its uncertainty. The source bootstrap resamples three streams, keeping both devices per stream; six timings are not six independent learning replicas. All timing trials, proposals and acceptances are retained. Temperature follows T(k)=u·0.01^(k/(cap−1)); changed caps also change annealing duration, while endpoints remain source-fixed. Both source and target timings synchronize around the complete solve call, including transfers and returned CPU arrays. Output scoring/serialization are outside solve timing but inside worker cost.')
    add();add('| Family | Fresh cohort seed | Clue counts 1 / 2 / 3 | Eligible unique inputs | Excluded historical/calibration/new-family keys | Compatible completions | Data SHA |');add('|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|')
    for f in s['family_results']:
        if'dataset'in f:
            d=f['dataset'];add(f"| {f['family']} | {d['input_seed']} | {d['by_clues']['1']} / {d['by_clues']['2']} / {d['by_clues']['3']} | {d['eligible_keys']:,} | {d['all_excluded_keys']:,} | {d['compatible_completions']:,} | `{d['data_sha256']}` |")
    add();add('All family caps/outcomes are sealed before cohort reservation. Each family excludes the entire final H3ac search/calibration exclusion history, H3ac’s own test keys, and the union of both new source-calibration key sets. The second family also excludes the first family’s newly reserved target keys. Cohorts therefore share no new target keys, and each has zero overlap with its full exclusion union. Every method within a family receives identical saved permutation starts for every input, chain and seed; there are 20 chains and search seeds 0/1/2. Initializer and GPU proposal random streams are separate. Physical-device assignment crosses methods/seeds on both GPUs.')
    add();add('| Family | Inputs with valid zero-F completion / 4,096 | Certified ceiling (%) | Compatible zero-F / all completions | Complete zero-F / full target bank | Given-given F conflicts |');add('|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|')
    for f in s['family_results']:
        if'exact_zero_set_capacity'in f:
            c=f['exact_zero_set_capacity'];add(f"| {f['family']} | {c['inputs_with_any_zero_conflict_completion']} | {c['certified_primary_ceiling_pct']:.6f} | {c['compatible_zero_conflict_completions']} / {c['total_compatible_completions']} | {c['valid_complete_target_solutions_with_zero_conflicts']} / {c['total_complete_target_solutions']} | {c['clues_with_internal_Fconflict_inputs']} |")
    add();add('Exact capacity is a ceiling for the abstaining certified primary; it does not bound valid energy fallback accuracy. Fallback and distinct valid solution coverage include capped returns and remain secondary. Supplied family geometry enters only independent dataset generation and diagnostic/audit calculations, never model weights, temperature or cap selection.')
    if s['output_diagnostics']:
        error=max(r['running_energy_absolute_error_max']for r in s['output_diagnostics']);changes=sum(r['exact_energy_certificate_count_change']!=0 for r in s['output_diagnostics']);wrong=sum(r['wrong_stops']for r in s['rows']);add();add(f"All **{s['audited_timed_target_states']:,} scored states** were audited for complete target membership, q/givens, permutation invariants, exact integer conflict counts, output selection, coverage, cap limits and direct float64 energy. There are **{wrong} wrong stopped chains**. Maximum running-energy error is **{error:.9f}**, below the frozen 0.1 gate. Exact-energy reselection changes correct certificate-first counts in **{changes} of {len(s['output_diagnostics'])}** scored jobs; all per-seed diagnostics remain tracked.")
    add();add(f"Total GPU-worker time is **{s['total_gpu_worker_seconds']:.6f} seconds ({s['total_gpu_worker_seconds']/60:.3f} GPU-minutes)**, with whole-study elapsed GPU-phase wall time **{s['whole_study_wall_seconds']:.6f} seconds**. The two timed fits total {s['fit_seconds_total']:.6f} seconds. Worker time by phase: {', '.join(f'{k}: {v:.6f}s'for k,v in s['worker_seconds_by_phase'].items())}. The separate 900-second wall/1,800 aggregate-worker-second envelope starts only after H3ac releases both GPUs. Fit/loss validation, calibration/refinement, full-shape 32-proposal warmups and scored target workers all count. There is no deadline reset. CPU preparation overlaps H3ac, but H3ad GPU work does not overlap it.")
    add();add('Calibration is included in total experimental cost and is not silently amortized away. The matched-time endpoint concerns scored solve calls after source selection, not the end-to-end cost to develop a recipe. These two fixed families retain the queens permutation structure; they do not establish transfer to tasks where that supplied structure is absent. This is a research derivative of the fitted energy and a prospective extension of the previous experiments, not a new reproduction claim for the paper.')
    add();add('[Frozen protocol](protocol.json), [complete enumeration gate](generate.py), [source producer and fitting](source.py), [source calibration](calibration.py), [fresh cohorts](prepare.py), [target runner](driver.py), [independent audit](analyze.py), [tracked summary](../../../../results/research/loki/h3ad/summary.json), [calibration receipts](../../../../results/research/loki/h3ad/calibration-selections.json), [per-input capacity](../../../../results/research/loki/h3ad/per-input-capacity.npz), [figure provenance](../../../../results/research/loki/h3ad/plot-provenance.json).')
